{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"94c932139eadee01","name":"card_unit_179th_tomahawks","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/USA/BrothersInArms/units/card_unit_179th_tomahawks","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"179th TOMAHAWKS","text":"Destruction: Add a copy of this unit to your support line. It becomes Veteran.","flavorText":"The 179th Infantry Regiment (nicknamed Tomahawks) was part of the 45th Infantry Division of the US Army during WWII. In 1943, the 179th Infantry Regiment, along with the rest of the 45th Infantry Division, was deployed to Europe. The regiment arrived in Italy in June 1943 and participated in the Allied campaign to liberate Italy from Axis control. The regiment fought in various battles and engagements throughout Italy. One of the notable actions in which the 179th Infantry Regiment participated was the Battle of Anzio, which took place from January to May 1944. The battle was a critical operation which aimed at breaking the stalemate of the Italian campaign and advancing towards Rome. After the Italian campaign, the regiment played a significant role in the Allied advance through France and into Germany and participated in major operations such as the Battle of the Bulge and the crossing of the Rhine River.","faction":"USA","type":"infantry","rarity":"Rare","cost":7,"operationCost":1,"attack":4,"defense":3},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_179th_tomahawks","title":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_179th_tomahawks_title","SourceString":"179th TOMAHAWKS","LocalizedString":"179th TOMAHAWKS"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":4,"defense":3,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::USA","kredits":7,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_unit_179th_tomahawks_text","SourceString":"Destruction: Add a copy of this unit to your support line. It becomes Veteran.","LocalizedString":"Destruction: Add a copy of this unit to your support line. It becomes Veteran."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key